---
description: Commit and push each completed project change
alwaysApply: true
---

- After completing a change, run the appropriate checks, commit the task's files, and push the current branch to origin before reporting completion.
- Push new branches with upstream tracking. Keep secrets, generated builds and unrelated user edits out of commits.
- Do not force-push or merge into another branch unless requested. If a commit or push fails, report the blocker and the local branch/commit state.
- Include the pushed branch and short commit ID in the completion message.
